Build requirements -- GNU/Linux
===============================

Debian and Ubuntu only: the rpm distributions have no sparc64 cross glibc. On
such a host use container/Containerfile (container/README).

Packages
--------
Debian/Ubuntu packages, and what they provide:

    gcc-sparc64-linux-gnu                 sparc64-linux-gnu-gcc, cross compiler
    binutils-sparc64-linux-gnu            cross as, ld, objcopy, size, readelf
    libgcc-[ver]-dev-sparc64-cross        cross libgcc
    libc6-dev-sparc64-cross               cross glibc, 64-bit, static
                                          (forth64, makedi, makeprom)
    libc6-dev-sparc-sparc64-cross         cross glibc, 32-bit, for OpenBoot
                                          (static; forth32)
    gcc-[ver]-multilib-sparc64-linux-gnu  cross gcc -m32 multilib, for OpenBoot
    lib32gcc-[ver]-dev-sparc64-cross      cross libgcc, 32-bit, for OpenBoot

    qemu-user-static                      qemu-sparc{64,32plus}-static
                                          for OpenBoot (QEMU_SPARC64=,
                                          QEMU_SPARC32= override)
    qemu-system-sparc                     qemu-system-sparc64, for the tests
                                          (QEMU= overrides)

    gcc                                   host compiler (for mdgen/mdlint and aschk)
    cpp                                   traditional cpp (-traditional-cpp)
    binutils                              ar
    make 4.3 or later (GNU)               grouped targets (`&:`) in build/obp/gnu/obp-gnu.mk
    patch, flex, python3, perl
    gawk, diffutils, coreutils            awk, cmp; od, sha256sum, dd

[ver] is the major version of gcc: 13 on Ubuntu 24.04. Built and tested with
gcc 13, 14, 15 and 16 (14 to 16 from source): build_matrix. Another gcc, or GCC
15 and later (C23): see README.configure, "Choosing the compiler".

Optional
--------
- ./configure checks that the tools above are present and usable before a build
  starts, and says what is missing: README.configure.
- git: without it the OpenBoot banner says "git unknown" instead of the commit
  id. `make release` needs it.
- Network: `make bootstrap-check` and `bootstrap-chain`
  (forth_bootstrap/README) clone cforth on the first run.

Versions this was built and tested with
---------------------------------------
    cross gcc, host gcc          13.3.0, 14.4.0, 15.3.0, 16.2.0 (build_matrix)
    cross binutils               2.42
    make                         4.3 (Ubuntu 24.04)
    flex                         2.6.4
    python3                      3.12.3
    qemu-sparc64 / -sparc32plus  8.2.2 (a linux-user build of QEMU from
                                 source gives byte-identical output)
    qemu-system-sparc            8.2.2, tests only
    glibc (32-bit, cross)        2.39

Little here depends on a specific version. GNU make must be 4.3 or later (grouped targets; an older one
stops with a message that says so). The other real constraint is that cpp
must support -traditional-cpp: the MD sources use K&R token pasting
(`cpu/**/x` in md/common.pdesc), which an ANSI preprocessor does not perform.
